---
import Presentation from "../../../../components/Presentation.astro";
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a
          href="/courses/eng-design-fab/"
          class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3"
        >
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Session 25: Field Test Day</h1>
        <p class="text-sn-theme">Racquet Ball Launcher Project &mdash; Milestone 5 of 6</p>
        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <!-- Launch / Concept -->
        <section id="launch">
          <Presentation>
            <section>
              <h2>Session 25</h2>
              <h3 class="text-sn-theme">Field Test Day</h3>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Today Is the Real Test</h2>
              <p>Not a lab day. Not a practice run.</p>
              <p class="fragment">
                Your calibration model gets tested for real, under
                pressure, with no do-overs.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate data-auto-animate-restart>
              <h2>How It Works</h2>
              <ol>
                <li class="fragment">You receive 1 target distance at a time &mdash; 3 total</li>
                <li class="fragment">Using only your model, choose your settings</li>
                <li class="fragment">Attempt the launch</li>
                <li class="fragment">Repeat for targets 2 and 3</li>
              </ol>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Margin of Error</h2>
              <p>
                <b class="text-sn-theme">&plusmn; 3 yards</b> &mdash; the
                same number you calibrated against back at the Session
                15&ndash;16 kickoff.
              </p>
              <p class="fragment">This has not changed.</p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate>
              <h2>What's Being Measured</h2>
              <p>Not your farthest throw.</p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate data-auto-animate-restart>
              <h2>What's Being Measured</h2>
              <p>
                <b class="text-sn-theme">Predictive accuracy</b> &mdash; can
                you hit an unknown target using only data you already
                collected?
              </p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>If You Miss</h2>
              <p>A miss is not the end of your grade.</p>
              <p class="fragment">
                How you explain it, next session, is worth just as much as
                hitting the target.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate data-auto-animate-restart>
              <h2>Before Your Attempt</h2>
              <ul>
                <li class="fragment">Know your usable range from Sessions 20&ndash;24</li>
                <li class="fragment">Bring your calibration curve/model with you</li>
                <li class="fragment">Agree as a team on your settings before you commit</li>
              </ul>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Safety Reminder</h2>
              <p>
                Bungee-cord protocols from Sessions 14&ndash;15 still apply
                on the field, not just in the makerspace.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>After Your 3 Attempts</h2>
              <p>
                Record your results &mdash; target, settings chosen, actual
                landing distance, hit or miss.
              </p>
              <p class="fragment">You'll need this for Session 26.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Next Up</h2>
              <p>Session 26: Reflect &amp; Defend</p>
              <p class="fragment">
                Explain your variable, your model, and your results &mdash;
                misses included.
              </p>
            </section>
          </Presentation>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Build -->
        <section id="build">
          <h2>Build</h2>

          <p>
            There's no build task today &mdash; today's "build" is the field
            test itself.
          </p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Your Recording Sheet</h3>
          <table class="table table-dark table-sm">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Target #</th>
                <th>Target Distance</th>
                <th>Settings Chosen</th>
                <th>Actual Landing Distance</th>
                <th>Hit / Miss</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>1</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>
              <tr><td>2</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>
              <tr><td>3</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>

          <p>
            Fill this in immediately after each attempt, not from memory
            later &mdash; you'll need accurate numbers, not impressions, for
            Session 26.
          </p>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Checkpoint -->
        <section id="checkpoint">
          <h2>Checkpoint</h2>

          <p>Before you leave the field, confirm:</p>

          <ul>
            <li>All 3 attempts are recorded, including any misses</li>
            <li>The settings you actually used are written down, not just the target and result</li>
            <li>Bungee safety protocols were followed on every attempt, not just the first</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Reflection -->
        <section id="reflection">
          <h2>Reflection</h2>

          <p>Answer these on your own. Reflections are individual, even when the rest of the session was team work.</p>

          <ol>
            <li>For any target you missed, what's your first guess at the cause &mdash; a limitation of your model, wind or field conditions, inconsistent execution, or something else? Say how you'd tell those apart.</li>
            <li>Session 26 asks you to defend your results either way. Which of today's three attempts do you think you'll have the most to say about?</li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Submit -->
        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>Submit your recording sheet and your reflection.</p>

          <h1
            class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash"
          >
            Milestone Complete
          </h1>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
